BIB                 11         28
TITLE      Investigation of alpha-particles interaction with
           zirconium: Cross-section measurements and isomeric
           cross-section ratios
AUTHOR     (A.Elbinawi,B.M.Ali,A.M.Zaghloul,M.Al-Abyad,F.Ditroi,
           N.El-anwar)
INSTITUTE  (3EGYCAI,3HUNDEB)
REFERENCE  (J,ARI,231,112510,2026)
           #doi:10.1016/j.apradiso.2026.112510
FACILITY   (CYCLO,3HUNDEB)
SAMPLE     High purity, 25 um thick, natural isotopic composition
           zirconium
DETECTOR   (HPGE)
METHOD     (ACTIV,STTA)
ERR-ANALYS (EN-ERR)
           Including the primary beam energy uncertainty and the
           uncertainty of target thickness
           (ERR-T)
           The total uncertainty of the cross-section values
            (12-21%) is estimated using the standard method, which
           involves taking the quadratic sum of the independently
           contributing parameters.
           (ERR-S,8.0,19.0) statistical uncertainty (8-19%)
           (ERR-1) beam intensity (7.0%)
           (ERR-2) target thickness (3.0%)
           (ERR-3) detection efficiency (5.0%)
           (ERR-4) half-life (3.0%)
